---
title: Charred broccolini with shallot salsa macha
servings: 1
tags: [vegan]
source: Charred broccolini, shallot salsa macha and fried shallots by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/charred-broccolini
---

> A restaurant batch: the shallots and salsa make far more than one plate needs.

== Fried shallots ==

Heat the @neutral oil{800%g} in a #saucepan{} over medium-high heat. Add the @shallots{400%g} and fry ~{5%minutes}, stirring now and then, until they start to brown.

Strain, keeping the oil. Spread the shallots on a #sheet tray{} lined with paper towels, season with @kosher salt{} and let cool.

== Shallot salsa macha ==

Put the saved shallot oil in a #saucepan{} over medium-high heat. Add the @pepitas{100%g} and cook, whisking often so they do not clump, until fragrant.

Take off the heat and add the @dried guajillo chiles{100%g}. Let cool.

Pulse in a #blender{} until the chiles are broken up but not smooth. Tip into a bowl, fold in three quarters of the fried shallots and season with @kosher salt{}.

== To serve ==

Char the @broccolini{} on all sides in a #cast-iron pan{} over medium-high heat.

Toss with as much salsa macha as you like, plate, and top with the rest of the fried shallots.
